 "info": {
  "description": "Bounded simulator subset of the official Amazon Forecast Service API (2018-06-26). Every other official operation returns HTTP 501 UnknownOperationException. Datasets and dataset groups are stored ACTIVE configuration records: no data is imported, nothing is stored in a dataset, and no predictor, forecast, explainability, monitor, what-if analysis, export or import job exists, so the Create, Describe, List and Delete operations of all of those, StopResource, ResumeResource, GetAccuracyMetrics and DeleteResourceTree return UnknownOperationException with HTTP 501. QueryForecast belongs to the separate forecastquery service and is not served. UpdateDatasetGroup is not implemented and CreateDatasetGroup refuses a non-empty DatasetArns, because a dataset group would have to resolve each dataset and compare its Domain with the group's, which the stored model cannot express. A dataset group therefore holds no datasets and reports no DatasetArns, and deleting a dataset never needs to update a group. A dataset is stored as given: the Domain and DatasetType combination, the fields the schema must contain for them (for example item_id, timestamp and demand for RETAIL and TARGET_TIME_SERIES) and the encryption role and key are not checked. DataFrequency is required for RELATED_TIME_SERIES datasets and must be an integer followed by min, H, D, W, M or Y within the documented range of that unit (min 1-59, H 1-23, D 1-6, W 1-4, M 1-11, Y 1). The engine first applies the official shape pattern, which as published lists only the literals Y, M, W, D, H, 30min, 15min, 10min, 5min and 1min, so only 1min, 5min, 10min, 15min and 30min are accepted here and values such as 1D or 2W that AWS accepts are refused with InvalidInputException. Dataset and dataset group names are unique per Region and Forecast limits are local: 100 datasets and 100 dataset groups per Region. Deleting a resource never fails with ResourceInUseException because nothing can use one. Tags follow the documented rules that keys must not start with aws: (any letter case) and that a resource holds at most 50; the length limits come from the official shapes. TagResource and UntagResource refuse keys with the reserved prefix.",
  "title": "Amazon Forecast (simulator catalog)",
  "version": "2018-06-26"
 },
